Chapter: GopWebSpawn
  cites Works chapter GopWeb

 THE FIRST SHIPPED CALLER OF `process-spawn`, graded. Everything this arm
 asks about is the SPAWN, not the webserver: whether a chapter outside
 `codex/test` can put a service in a process of its own, whether an
 application processor actually runs it, and whether the parent survives
 doing so.

 Cell 36200 is `ap-dispatch-count-addr` and it is the instrument, because
 it counts processes claimed by a core whose id is NOT zero. The boot
 processor is always core zero, so a value above zero cannot have been
 written by the parent: it is evidence that some other core took a process
 out of the table and ran it. Nothing here has to trust that the child
 reached any particular line of the server.

 THE SABOTAGE THIS ARM EXISTS FOR: delete the `gopweb-start` line and the
 dispatch count must stay at nought. An arm that still reports a dispatch
 without the spawn is measuring the parent, which is the whole failure the
 design warned about.

 The parent spins after spawning rather than waiting, because a service
 does not exit and a `process-wait` on one would never return. The spin is
 also the second half of the acceptance: the parent is still running its
 own code while the child has the network.

 IT WAITS FOR THE DISPATCH RATHER THAN SAMPLING FOR IT, and that is not a
 detail. A claim does not happen at the moment of the spawn: an idle core
 has to come round its scan and take the entry. Read once after a single
 spin, this arm said NO AP RAN THE SERVICE while the service was perfectly
 healthy, and that reads exactly like a capability failure. Three children
 spawned in one run and counted separately are what showed the count simply
 lagging. A bounded wait turns a race into a decidable question, and the
 bound is what makes the failure honest: not "never", but "not within this
 many spins".

Section: Body

  spin : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spin (n) (acc) = if n == 0 then acc else spin (n - 1) (acc + 1)

 The `s < 0` can never hold. It is there so the spin's result is READ, and
 a spin whose value nothing looks at is a spin the compiler may drop.

  wait-dispatch : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  wait-dispatch (tries) (before) =
    if tries <= 0 then atomic-load 36200
    else if atomic-load 36200 > before then atomic-load 36200
    else let s = spin 100000000 0
    in if s < 0 then 0 else wait-dispatch (tries - 1) before

  opening : [Console, Concurrent, Capability, Network.Read, Network.Write] Nothing = act
    let before = atomic-load 36200
    in act
      print-line-uni ("dispatched before " & show before)
      pid <- gopweb-start
      print-line-uni ("spawned " & show (pid > 0))
      let after = wait-dispatch 20 before
      in act
        print-line-uni ("parent still running " & show (spin 1000 0 == 1000))
        print-line-uni (if after > before
                        then "an ap ran the service"
                        else "NO AP RAN THE SERVICE")
        k <- process-kill pid
        print-line-uni ("service stopped " & show (k >= 0))
      end
    end
  end
